    "ONE representative genome per organism. Within-organism variation is not measured, so an organism-level claim rests on a single assembly for that organism -- except for E. coli, which has two (reference and draft) and is the only substrate with any internal replicate.",
    "The non-reference genomes are DRAFT assemblies from the AMR cohorts: contig-level, a different annotation pipeline, and a clinical-isolate sampling frame rather than a type strain. The reference-against-draft E. coli pair is included specifically so that confound is visible rather than assumed away.",
    "An upstream window is a PROXY for a promoter, not a mapped transcription start site, and that proxy is weaker in compact AT-rich genomes where overlap with the preceding CDS is common. The overlap fraction is reported per substrate for exactly that reason.",
