    "GC content is CONFOUNDED WITH PHYLOGENY in this substrate set: the two low-GC genomes are both Campylobacter and the three high-GC genomes are all Enterobacteriaceae. The margin-against-GC correlation is therefore a two-group comparison with an effective n of 2, not a five-point regression, and is reported only as a description of this table. Reading it as a GC effect would repeat the lineage confound that has already closed four arms in this project. Separating GC from lineage needs substrates that cross them -- a high-GC Campylobacter or a low-GC enterobacterium -- which this set does not contain.",
